title: The Ha Giang Loop — what four days really cost, every dong (2026)
format: story
charstyle: nutshell
voice: af_heart
music: adventure
score: adventure@1 night@2 upbeat@3 tension@4 adventure@5 night@6 wonder@7 tension@8 emotional@9 upbeat@10 adventure@11
sources: Vietadvisor "Ha Giang Loop Cost" receipt, Sep 2026 (sleeper cabin 350k each way, standard sleeper 250k; XR150 450–600k/day; semi-auto ~200k/day; border permit 230k; fuel ~11 L 250k; homestays 300–350k, Dong Van room with dinner and breakfast ~300k; dinner 100–150k; lunch 40–60k; food & drinks 1.17M; Lung Cu 25k + 10k parking; Nho Que boat 150k; total 5,285,000 VND ≈ $203; budget version ≈ 3.7M ≈ $141; damage fees $50–300; easy rider $190–230 for 4 days, tip $10–20/day, ≈ $280–320 from Hanoi; 3M VND cash; ATMs Ha Giang city, Dong Van, Meo Vac; avoid sub-$100 tours); Tuoi Tre News 15 Apr 2026 (350 km loop; after a British tourist died on an easy rider trip in early April, licensed operators must provide maintained vehicles, helmets and protective gear; unlicensed companies may not sell tours); vietnamtourism.com "Ha Giang Loop — the honest 2026 guide" (riding without a valid licence: fine 4–5M VND; zero-alcohol breath tests; fog under 10 m Nov–Feb); zinghomehagiang.com permit guide (230–300k). Checked Oct 2026.
// YOUTUBE CUT (16:9): one continuous trip, no chapters — the night bus, the town, the road, the homestay, the canyon, the twist
//         (no licence → easy rider), the receipt, the cheap version, the save card. Re-hooks: the checkpoint (0:55), the twist (2:05).
// VIRAL   odometer cold open; "keep a guess in your head" (comment bait); mid-point twist; $3 over; budget version; Hoi An tease.

// 0:00 ECU odometer 000 → 350, WHIP OUT: Dave rides the mountain road; "UNDER $200?"; tape 350 KM; "4 DAYS"; "COUNT IT!".
# vis kind=hg act=hook
This is Dave. Dave wants to ride the Ha Giang Loop for under two hundred dollars.
Three hundred and fifty kilometres of mountain road. Four days.
We're going to count every single dong. Keep a guess in your head.
// 0:15 ZOOM THROUGH the headlight into night: the sleeper bus over moonlit karst, Dave asleep; +350K; "STANDARD 250K"; brakes;
//      "4:00 AM"; dawn creeps in; the driver says stay till eight.
# vis kind=hg act=bus spent=350000 adds="350000@0" stdCap=1 arriveCap=2 stayCap=3 trans=zoomthru tc=.6,.62
It starts with the night bus from Hanoi. A sleeper cabin is three hundred and fifty thousand dong.
The ordinary sleeper is two hundred and fifty.
It rolls into Ha Giang at around four in the morning.
Some cabin companies let you stay on board until eight, so you don't pay for a room you'd use for three hours.
// 0:36 BLOOM into dawn: the rental shop; Dave weighs the bikes, picks the XR150 (+1.8M), SNAP SNAP SNAP, permit stamp (+230K).
# vis kind=hg act=rent spent=2380000 adds="1800000@2|230000@4" trans=bloom tc=.5,.3 tcol=#ffd98a
In Ha Giang city, a Honda XR150 rents for four hundred and fifty to six hundred thousand a day.
A semi-automatic is about two hundred. If you don't ride a clutch at home, that's the better bike up here.
Dave rides a manual at home, so it's the XR150. Four days: one point eight million.
Photograph every scratch. Damage fees of fifty to three hundred dollars are where cheap shops make their money.
Then the border permit for the zone around Lung Cu: two hundred and thirty thousand, with your passport.
// 1:08 WHIP to the checkpoint: skid, "Licence?", pocket panic, "FINE: MILLIONS / NO INSURANCE", PHEW, barrier up.
# vis kind=hg act=check spent=2380000 trans=whip
But at the first checkpoint, the officer wants one thing.
A licence Vietnam recognises.
Ride without one, and it's a fine of millions of dong, and an insurer that won't pay if anything happens.
Dave has his. Phew.
// 1:25 SLICES onto the road: hairpins, "DAY 1", tape 100 KM, the pump slides in, GLUG (+250K), a bowl of pho by the road.
# vis kind=hg act=ride spent=2630000 adds="250000@1" lunchCap=2 trans=slices
Day one: about a hundred kilometres, from Ha Giang city to Yen Minh.
The loop burns around eleven litres of fuel. Two hundred and fifty thousand.
Lunch on the road is a bowl of pho or a plate of rice, forty to sixty thousand.
// 1:40 BLOBS into night: the clay homestay, dinner, "LIMIT: 0", tea, laughter (+950K for three nights).
# vis kind=hg act=stay spent=3580000 adds="950000@0" dinnerCap=2 wineCap=3 teaCap=4 trans=blobs
Nights are homestays: three hundred to three hundred and fifty thousand for a private room.
In Dong Van, a room with dinner and breakfast can be about three hundred.
Dinner with the family is usually one hundred to one hundred and fifty.
The corn wine is free, and it keeps coming. But checkpoints run breath tests, and the limit for riders is zero.
So Dave says thank you, and sticks to tea.
// 2:05 MATCH steam into cloud: Ma Pi Leng; the boat far below (+150K); the flag tower (+35K); fog, 10 M, ride slow.
# vis kind=hg act=pass spent=3765000 adds="150000@1|35000@2" lungCap=2 fogCap=3 trans=match tc=.5,.55 tc2=.5,.4
Day three: Ma Pi Leng, the road cut into the cliffs above the Nho Que river.
Down in the canyon, the boat ride is one hundred and fifty thousand.
Up north, the Lung Cu flag tower is twenty-five thousand, plus ten to park the bike.
And from November to February, fog can drop visibility below ten metres in minutes. Ride slow.
// 2:28 SPIN into the twist: Dave's licence goes POOF; an easy rider pulls up; Dave on the back; "$190–230"; a roadside helmet
//      check, "APRIL 2026"; "≈ $280–320" + TIP.
# vis kind=hg act=rider trans=spin
But what if Dave didn't have that licence?
Then the answer is an easy rider: a local driver, and you ride on the back.
Four days cost one hundred and ninety to two hundred and thirty dollars, with fuel, beds, meals and the permit included.
After a fatal accident in April 2026, licensed companies must provide maintained bikes, helmets and protective gear, and unlicensed ones can't sell tours.
Add the bus and a tip of ten to twenty dollars a day, and it's about two hundred and eighty to three hundred and twenty from Hanoi.
// 3:00 ZOOM THROUGH into the bus window at night: the receipt unrolls; FOOD 1.17M (+1.17M, +350K bus home); "5,285,000 VND"; "$203"; +$3.
# vis kind=hg act=sum spent=5285000 adds="350000@0|1170000@1" foodCap=1 totalCap=2 usdCap=3 trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.5
Back to Dave, on the night bus home, adding it all up.
Food, coffee and drinks over four days: one point one seven million.
The total: five million, two hundred and eighty-five thousand dong.
About two hundred and three dollars. Three over… worth it.
// 3:18 WHIP to the cheap version: the bike swaps (−1M), a dorm bunk pops (−400K), a standard bus passes (−200K), "≈ $141".
# vis kind=hg act=budget spent=3685000 adds="-1000000@1|-400000@2|-200000@3" trans=whip
Want it cheaper? Three swaps.
A semi-automatic saves a million.
Dorm beds save about four hundred thousand.
The ordinary bus saves two hundred.
That's about three million seven hundred thousand. Around one hundred and forty-one dollars.
// 3:35 SLICES to the roadside: cash, ATM boards, the easy rider; "SKIP <$100 TOURS".
# vis kind=hg act=rules trans=slices last="SKIP TOURS UNDER $100"
Save this: bring three million dong in cash for the road.
ATMs are only in Ha Giang city, Dong Van and Meo Vac.
And skip the under-one-hundred-dollar tours. The saving comes out of the helmet, the bike and the driver.
// 3:50 ZOOM THROUGH a lantern: Hoi An at dusk.
# vis kind=hg act=tease trans=zoomthru tc=.5,.45
Next time, Dave heads south… to Hoi An.
